eed to find the area of triangle $PBD$.\n\n3. According to the properties of parallelograms, the following relationships hold:\n    - $S_{\\triangle P D G} = S_{\\triangle P B F}$,\n    - $S_{\\triangle P D E} = S_{\\triangle P B H}$,\n    - $S_{\\triangle B C D} = S_{\\triangle B A D}$.\n\n4. We can use these relationships to relate the areas of the parallelograms and triangles. We start by looking at the difference between the areas of the two given parallelograms:\n   \\[\n   S_{\\text{parallelogram } P E C G} - S_{\\text{parallelogram } A H P E}\n   \\]\n\n5. Expanding each area with the areas of associated triangles, we get:\n   \\[\n   S_{\\text{parallelogram } P E C G} + S_{\\triangle P D G} + S_{\\triangle P B F} - \\left( S_{\\text{parallelogram } A H P E} + S_{\\triangle P D E} + S_{\\triangle P B H} \\right)\n   \\]\n\n6. Knowing the relationships between triangles and using the property of congruent triangles in parallelograms, we simplify this to:\n   \\[\n   S_{\\text{four-sided shape } P B C D} - S_{\\text{four-sided shape } P B A D}\n   \\]\n   Since $ PBGD $ is directly opposite to $PBAD$, this further simplifies:\n   \\[\n   (S_{\\triangle B C D} + S_{\\triangle P B D}) - (S_{\\triangle B A D} + S_{\\triangle P B D}) = S_{\\triangle P B D} \\times 2\n   \\]\n\n7. Dividing both sides by 2, we find the area of $\\triangle P B D$:\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle P B D} = \\frac{S_{\\text{parallelogram } P E C G} - S_{\\text{parallelogram } A H P E}}{2}\n   \\]\n\n8. Substituting the known values:\n   \\[\n   S_{\\triangle P B D} = \\frac{16 - 5}{2} = \\frac{11}{2} = 5.5 \\text{ square centimeters}\n   \\]\n\n9. Therefore, the area of triangle $PBD$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5.5 \\text{ square centimeters}}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "The equation \\(5x + 3y = 71\\) has non-negative integer solutions of the form:\n\\[\n\\left\\{\n\\begin{array}{l}\nx_{1} = \\alpha_{1}, \\\\\ny_{1} = \\be